<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>PAYE tax bands for resident individuals, from 1 July 2023 (Kenya Revenue Authority; Finance Act 2023):</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Monthly taxable pay (Ksh)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Rate</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">First <m>24\,000</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>10\%</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Next <m>8333</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>25\%</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Next <m>467\,667</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>30\%</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Next <m>300\,000</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>32.5\%</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Above <m>800\,000</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>35\%</m></cell></row></tabular><p>Personal relief: Ksh <m>2400</m> a month, taken off the tax. PAYE is never negative.</p><p>Achieng's taxable pay rises from Ksh <m>{26\,000}</m> to Ksh <m>{34\,000}</m> a month. The other deductions on the payslip do not change. Achieng says: <q>Now I am in the <m>30\%</m> band, so all my pay is taxed at <m>30\%</m> and I will take home less than before.</q></p><p>(a) Find the PAYE before the rise.</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans1"/>  </p><p>(b) Find the PAYE after the rise.</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans2"/>  </p><p>(c) Which statement is right?</p><p/><ol marker="(1)">
<li>Achieng is right: all of the pay is now taxed at 30%, so take-home pay falls.</li>
<li>Achieng is wrong: only the part of the pay above Ksh 32 333 is taxed at 30%, so take-home pay rises.</li>
<li>Achieng is right: personal relief is lost on moving into a higher band.</li>
<li>Achieng is wrong: the rate of tax does not depend on how much you earn.</li>
</ol>  <p>(d) By how much does take-home pay change? Type a negative number for a fall.</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans4"/>  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) Before: tax <m>= 2400 + 25\% \times ({26\,000} - 24\,000) = {2900}</m>; PAYE <m>= {2900} - 2400 = {500}</m>.</p><p>(b) After: tax <m>= 2400 + 2083.25 + 30\% \times ({34\,000} - 32\,333) = {4983.35}</m>; PAYE <m>= {2583.35}</m>.</p><p>(c) Each slice of pay is taxed at its own band's rate, so a rise never lowers take-home pay. Only the part above <m>32\,333</m> pays <m>30\%</m>; personal relief stays Ksh <m>2400</m>.</p><p>(d) The pay rises by <m>{8000}</m> and PAYE by <m>{2583.35} - {500} = {2083.35}</m>, so take-home pay rises by <m>{8000} - {2083.35} = {5916.65}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>500.0</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>2583.35</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>(2)</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>5916.65</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>